1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:05,286
Today we cross the Rockies on I-70!

2
00:00:05,286 --> 00:00:09,024
A Victorian mining town with a sky-high railroad bridge.

3
00:00:09,024 --> 00:00:13,096
One of the most beautiful stretches of interstate in America.

4
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:16,300
And a giant hot springs pool waiting at the end!

5
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:25,024
This is Denver to Glenwood Springs: 157 miles over the Continental Divide, from the Mile High City to the hot springs.

6
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:28,450
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,465
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:30,465 --> 00:00:40,520
We leave Denver, stop in Georgetown, tunnel under the Continental Divide, stop in Frisco and Vail, drive Glenwood Canyon, and soak in Glenwood Springs!

9
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:44,485
We're starting in Denver, the Mile High City!

10
00:00:44,485 --> 00:00:49,375
There's even a step on the State Capitol marked at exactly one mile high.

11
00:00:49,375 --> 00:00:51,720
Okay, let's head for the mountains!

12
00:00:52,670 --> 00:01:00,240
Up into the foothills on I-70, and past Idaho Springs, one of Colorado's very first gold rush towns.

13
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:02,360
The mountains close in fast!

14
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:07,298
Welcome to Georgetown, a perfectly preserved Victorian mining town!

15
00:01:07,298 --> 00:01:13,370
Ride the Georgetown Loop Railroad over the Devil's Gate High Bridge, ninety-five feet above the creek!

16
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:19,599
Now we drive straight under the Continental Divide, through the Eisenhower Tunnel!

17
00:01:19,599 --> 00:01:26,810
At eleven thousand one hundred fifty-eight feet, it's the highest point on the entire Interstate Highway System!

18
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:34,074
Welcome to Frisco, right on the shore of Dillon Reservoir, with the Tenmile Range towering over town.

19
00:01:34,074 --> 00:01:36,200
Walk Main Street and grab a snack!

20
00:01:37,150 --> 00:01:44,034
Up and over Vail Pass, ten thousand six hundred sixty-two feet, and down the other side into Vail.

21
00:01:44,034 --> 00:01:45,580
Use those lower gears!

22
00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:47,550
Welcome to Vail!

23
00:01:47,550 --> 00:01:51,884
It looks like a little European village tucked under the Gore Range.

24
00:01:51,884 --> 00:01:56,410
Stroll Vail Village and Lionshead, and ride the gondola for a big view!

25
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,042
And now, the best part!

26
00:01:59,042 --> 00:02:04,672
I-70 squeezes into Glenwood Canyon, with the Colorado River right beside you.

27
00:02:04,672 --> 00:02:08,036
Hike to Hanging Lake if you can grab a permit.

28
00:02:08,036 --> 00:02:09,060
It's stunning!

29
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:14,499
This is Glenwood Canyon, with cliffs towering over the Colorado River.

30
00:02:14,499 --> 00:02:18,988
Engineers stacked the highway in layers to squeeze it into the canyon.

31
00:02:18,988 --> 00:02:22,130
Pull off at Grizzly Creek and walk the bike path!

32
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:25,732
Out of the canyon and into town.

33
00:02:25,732 --> 00:02:26,810
Time to soak!

34
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:30,244
We made it to Glenwood Springs!

35
00:02:30,244 --> 00:02:35,451
The hot springs pool here is huge, and it's been open since 1888.

36
00:02:35,451 --> 00:02:38,656
And fun fact: Doc Holliday from the O.K.

37
00:02:38,656 --> 00:02:41,540
Corral is buried right here in town!

38
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:44,322
And that's the drive!

39
00:02:44,322 --> 00:02:52,610
157 miles from Denver to Glenwood Springs, topping out at 11,158 feet in the Eisenhower Tunnel.

40
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:56,720
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

41
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,490
Pause and grab a screenshot!

42
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:03,656
Thanks for riding along!

43
00:03:03,656 --> 00:03:10,440
Hit subscribe, and next time we're heading west to the red rock canyons of Colorado National Monument!
